{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>You shall not do after all that we do here, etc.</b> This is connected back to <b>for you are crossing the Jordan, etc.</b>: When you cross the Jordan you are immediately permitted to sacrifice on a bāmāh all the fourteen years of conquest and division. But on the bāmāh you shall not offer everything that you offer <b>here today</b> in the Mishkan — which is with you, anointed, and fit for offering sin-offerings and guilt-offerings, vows and freewill-offerings upon it. But on a bāmāh only the vow and the freewill-offering are brought — and that is <b>every man whatsoever is right in his own eyes</b>: vows and freewill-offerings that you volunteer because it seems right in your eyes to bring them, not by obligation — those you may offer on the bāmāh (ibid.; Zevaḥim 117)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:44.351783836Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}